WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
Rapping up the week on Tesla's short time, Episode 530.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.700
Patrick here in Vancouver, its July 3, 2026.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.560
Let's close out the week with today's Tesla news.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.820
Tesla posted its fourth best quarter ever

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.440
with 480,126 deliveries.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.140
But the stock still dropped 7.5%.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.460
Tesla reported 451,758 vehicles produced

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:32.760
in the second quarter, along with 480,126 deliveries.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:37.140
The company also deployed 13.5 gigawatt hours

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.240
of energy storage during the period.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.220
These figures mark the fourth best quarter

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.480
in Tesla history for vehicle deliveries.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.500
The results exceeded forecasts and triggered gains

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.840
in shares of Chinese suppliers tied to Tesla production.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.280
Tesla will stream its full second quarter update

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:58.820
live on X on July 22 at 4.30 pm central time.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.560
While the overall delivery numbers show broad recovery,

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.320
one specific product launch is expanding Tesla's US SUV lineup.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.320
Tesla began US sales of the six-seat Model Y L variant

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.740
with an extended wheelbase.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:18.920
The launch series edition is priced at $61,990

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.640
and includes specific interior upgrades.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.380
The Model Y L launch series features door trim puddle lights,

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.200
a suede dashboard wing, exclusive badging, floor mats,

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:31.200
and sill plates.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.260
The model offers an extended wheelbase

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.400
for more interior space and a 325 mile range.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.560
It has been available in China since last year

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.640
and is now offered in the United States and Puerto Rico.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.500
As Tesla adds new variants at home,

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.680
it is also navigating shifting competitive positions

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:51.060
abroad.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.160
China's BYD surpassed Tesla to regain lead

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.760
in global EV race.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:02.020
BYD overtook Tesla again in global EV sales volume

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:02.840
during the quarter.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.480
Tesla still posted strong growth.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.460
BYD's broader lineup and domestic strength allowed it

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.960
to reclaim the top spot.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.020
The shift underscores ongoing competition

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:15.860
in the worldwide EV market.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.700
South China Morning Post covered the change

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.480
in the global EV race.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.840
The Hyundai Ionic 5 increased sales year over year

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.220
while several other non-Tesla EVs saw declines.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.520
It now holds the top position among EVs

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.120
excluding Tesla models in the US market.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.160
The gain highlights shifting buyer preferences

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.980
among non-Tesla options.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.420
Inside EVs reported the updated ranking

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.620
based on recent US sales data.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.300
The Ionic 5 achieved the lead

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.560
through stronger year over year performance.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.940
Other non-Tesla models recorded sales declines

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:53.960
in the same period.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.660
This places the Ionic 5 as the leading option

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.240
outside the Tesla lineup.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.340
The same competitive pressure is visible in individual markets

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.340
where policy support is changing.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.980
Tesla increased model Y prices in South Korea

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.980
following government approval of subsidies for the vehicle.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.800
The adjustment came after the company captured 30%

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.880
of imported car sales in the market.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.420
Sales have risen sharply since the subsidy decision.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.260
Tesla vehicles now account for 30%

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.940
of all imported cars sold in South Korea.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.240
The model Y in particular dominates the imported segment.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:34.660
Strong demand followed the recent subsidy approval

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:35.800
and price adjustments.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:40.500
Business Korea and electric-vehicles.com both reported

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.600
on the price changes and market share.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.320
South Korea is not the only market

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.660
showing strong Tesla demand this quarter.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.960
The model Y set a new single month sales record in Australia.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:56.920
Combined Tesla and BYD EV sales helped push electric vehicles

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:00.020
to 23.4% of the overall market.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.460
The result reflects continued strong demand in the region.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.800
Bassonore noted the record for the model Y.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:10.600
Tesla and BYD together drove the monthly totals.

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:13.900
The combined volumes lifted the electric segment

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.260
past earlier peaks.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.040
Google News carried the report on the Australian market share.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.580
Volume momentum is also pushing Tesla

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.800
toward a major cumulative milestone.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:28.560
Tesla is on pace to hit 10 million cumulative vehicle sales

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.940
during the current quarter.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:35.160
The second quarter delivery total of 480,126

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.880
contributed to this milestone.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:40.420
Cumulative figures track total vehicles delivered

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.740
since production began.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.640
Clean Technica projected the 10 million threshold based

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:46.700
on the latest deliveries.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.660
Not every story this week is about growth.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.940
One incident drew legal attention.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.680
Authorities charged the driver of a Tesla

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:57.760
involved in a fatal Florida crash with manslaughter.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.480
The case centers on driver actions

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.240
rather than vehicle systems.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.520
Details remain limited pending further investigation.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.600
Tesla Roddy posted the update from Florida authorities.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.840
Before we wrap the main news,

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:15.680
here is a closer look at how subsidies affect pricing decisions.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.340
Subsidies in markets like South Korea

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.580
alter the effective transaction price

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.000
more directly than most product changes.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.900
When approval arrives,

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.000
Tesla can raise the posted price

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.660
without losing buyer interest

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.380
because the net cost to the customer stays similar or improves.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:36.000
The adjustment reveals how much of the original price

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.120
already incorporated expected incentive levels

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.160
rather than pure production costs.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.180
This dynamic differs from pure technology-driven price

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:48.040
reductions, which reflect falling component costs

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.740
or manufacturing scale.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:53.800
In South Korea, the move followed subsidy confirmation

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.740
and coincided with Tesla claiming 30%

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.320
of imported vehicle sales.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.860
The sequence shows pricing power

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:04.560
tied to policy timing instead of internal efficiencies alone.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.100
For the business, the pattern affects

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.180
gross margin visibility and demand forecasting.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.220
Companies must decide whether to lock in higher list prices

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.760
once incentives appear or keep headroom

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:18.280
for future policy shifts.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.060
Watching how Tesla manages this balance

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:23.040
in additional markets will clarify

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.180
whether subsidy linked pricing becomes a recurring tool

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.720
or a temporary response.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.320
Strong second quarter results sent shares

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.860
of Chinese companies supplying Tesla higher.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:37.480
The delivery beat created immediate positive movement

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:40.340
and supplier equities tied to Tesla production.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.140
Investors viewed the 480,126 figure

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:47.400
as confirmation of sustained demand.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:51.620
The reaction shows how Tesla's volume directly influences

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.520
its upstream partners in China.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.840
Google News tracked the supplier's share gains

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.460
following the delivery release.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:02.600
Shares fell sharply even after the strong delivery report.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.160
Traders appear focused on an unspecified July 7 event

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:08.920
rather than the quarterly volume.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:12.660
The price action shows how forward-looking catalysts

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.440
can override near-term results.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.600
Market participants are watching for details

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.360
on what the announcement may cover.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:24.820
Morningstar noted the 7.5% decline despite the volume beat.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:29.100
Both Tesla and BYD set new monthly records in Australia.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:33.380
EV market share climbed to 23.4%,

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:36.820
driven by strong model Y and BYD volumes.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.540
The result marks a notable step in Australia's shift

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:41.940
toward electric vehicles.

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:44.480
Combined sales from the two companies

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.980
pushed the segment higher than previous peaks.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.480
Google News reported the combined record month.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.760
A Chinese EV executive publicly ranked Tesla's

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:58.220
FSD as the sole first tier autonomous system.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.000
The comment singled out Tesla's approach

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.140
above other competitors in the market.

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:06.000
It highlights perceived technical leadership

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.940
in supervised autonomy from an industry insider.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.600
The statement adds to ongoing debate

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.740
about relative capabilities across global players.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.900
Google News carried the executives ranking of FSD.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.440
Tesla shares declined 7.5%,

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:27.100
even after reporting 480,126 deliveries

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.860
and 25% year-over-year growth.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:34.680
Investors focused instead on an unspecified July 7 announcement

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.780
and broader valuation concerns.

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.980
The reaction shows that strong volume alone

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:42.480
does not guarantee positive stock movement

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.820
when other catalysts dominate sentiment.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.480
Morningstar highlighted the disconnect between deliveries

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.060
and the share price reaction.

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:52.860
Tomorrow, we will be watching for any details

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.260
that emerge about the July 7 announcement

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.640
and how it may shape near-term sentiment.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.800
That's your Tesla news for today.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:04.740
TSLA closed at $393.45,

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:09.760
down $31.85, 7.5%.

